# Normalize line endings to LF for every text file, on every platform,
# regardless of each contributor's local core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Why: this repo has been edited from both Windows (native CRLF-leaning
# tools) and Linux/macOS environments. Without this file, git relies on
# each clone's local core.autocrlf config to decide how line endings are
# handled, which is inconsistent across contributors and tools — the
# same unmodified file can show up as "changed" (CRLF vs LF) depending on
# who last touched it. `eol=lf` pins the checked-out line ending to LF
# for text files no matter what, so `git status` only shows real changes.
* text=auto eol=lf
